                <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px;color:#1B5E20'&gt;How it works&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gate junction&lt;/b&gt; = one solder joint shared by: GREEN wire (T13/BCM 27), one leg of the 4.7kΩ, and the MOSFET Gate pin. The 4.7kΩ other leg goes to T17 (+3.3V). The 4.7kΩ is a &lt;b&gt;pull-up in parallel at the gate&lt;/b&gt; — it is NOT in series with the green wire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Fire:&lt;/b&gt; software drives BCM 27 LOW → gate pulled to 0V → MOSFET OFF → solenoid de-energizes. BCM 27 released/HIGH → 4.7kΩ holds gate at 3.3V → MOSFET ON.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pump:&lt;/b&gt; BCM 17 → Relay CH1 switches +12V to the R385 pump (independent path).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#1565C0'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Bench check:&lt;/b&gt; probe the &lt;b&gt;gate junction&lt;/b&gt; (not T13). It should swing ~0V ↔ ~3.3V during Click Test. The T13 end of the green reading ~1.6V is normal.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F1F8E9;strokeColor=#4CAF50;fontColor=#333;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="760" width="1330" height="200" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
